# Fictional Band Name: The Hinged Choir

## Band Description

The Hinged Choir is a four-member ensemble built around the idea that non-vocal materials can speak without being disguised as voices.

**Iris Venn** — daxophone, interchangeable tongues, bowed friction, pressure bends, contact-mic routing.

**Malik “Mali” Batiste** — bounce drums, claps, chopped room triggers, mono sub, live pattern resets.

**Nia Rook** — prepared Wurlitzer, muted-key percussion, harmonic stabs, mechanical key noise.

**Solomon Reed** — bass harmonica, bent low notes, chordal breaths, reed chatter, hand percussion.

There is no conventional vocalist. Iris supplies the most voice-like material, but the ensemble treats speech as a rhythmic property rather than a lyrical requirement. Malik turns gestures into repeatable cells, Nia frames them harmonically, and Solomon adds breath and phrasing that can make the whole ensemble resemble a fragmented choir without anyone singing.

